# The snapshot the `identity` track's models actually transcribe.
#
# Every published result about the identity track is a statement about THIS snapshot and no
# other. It is the answer to "which version of EXTENSION-IDENTITY was verified?", and it is
# deliberately a separate fact from "which snapshots have been vendored."
#
# Vendoring a newer snapshot does NOT move this. It moves only after the models have been
# re-validated against the newer text, and moving it is the LAST step of that work. A pin
# that advances when someone copies files in would quietly convert "we vendored the new
# spec" into "we verified the new spec," which are not the same claim.
#
# WRITING THIS FILE IS WHAT PROMOTED THE TRACK, for the second time and by the same gate.
# `identity` was `status = "scoped"` in TRACKS.toml, and a scoped track is gated to carry no
# models and no pin -- adding a model file fails `make trackcheck` until the track is promoted
# WITH a pin. `quorum` was promoted this way on 2026-09-07 and this is the second instance;
# the gate has now forced the "say out loud which snapshot the results will be about" step
# twice, on two different days, without anyone having to remember it. That is what a gate is
# for and it is worth recording that it ran as designed rather than being worked around.
#
# THIS IS THE LAST TRACK TRACKS.toml SCOPES. With identity modeled there is no `scoped` track
# left, so the `scoped` gate now has NO subject -- it is teeth-tested by nothing until a fifth
# track is scoped. Recorded here rather than discovered later: a gate whose input set has gone
# empty asserts nothing, and this one asserts nothing from today. Its teeth-test is in
# tools/trackcheck.py's own test path, not in the live registry.
#
# This is the identity track's pin and it is independent of the other three. Core is held at
# v0.8.2 pending the keystone sibling's convergence and that has no bearing here.
# EXTENSION-IDENTITY v3.10 declares `Depends: ENTITY-CORE-PROTOCOL.md (v7.40+);
# EXTENSION-ATTESTATION.md (v1.2+); EXTENSION-QUORUM.md (v1.2+)` -- all three FLOORS, and all
# three met by the snapshots already vendored (`spec-data/v0.8.2` carries v7.62-v7.76 clause
# tags; `ext-attestation-v1.3` clears the v1.2 floor; `ext-quorum-v1.2` meets it exactly).
# The tracks pin independently by design.
#
# IDENTITY MODELS CITE BOTH SUBSTRATE SPECS, AND MORE HEAVILY THAN QUORUM CITED ONE. §3.5 is a
# table of nothing but substrate calls and §3.6's validators are composed almost entirely out
# of them, so the identity results depend on THREE pins at once: this file,
# MODELING-PIN-ATTESTATION and MODELING-PIN-QUORUM. Those citations are written `§ATTEST:4.3`
# and `§QUORUM:4.2`, which are excluded from every track's coverage set. They are still a real
# dependency: an identity result is a statement about all three snapshots, and moving any one
# of them invalidates it. Nothing gates that triple; it is stated here because the file a
# reader checks for "which version was verified" is this one.
#
# TWO OF THIS TRACK'S FINDINGS ARE CROSS-SPEC AND ONE OF THEM IS *ABOUT* THE PIN TRIPLE.
# EXTENSION-ATTESTATION's TV-A8 delegates the rejection of an invalid-signature revocation to
# "identity's `identity_verify_cert` ... at topology-dispatch step", and EXTENSION-IDENTITY
# §3.6 rejects every `kind="revocation"` before topology dispatch is reached. Neither document
# is wrong when read alone. That defect exists only in the pair, which is precisely the class
# a per-document pin cannot express -- so read this paragraph as the reason the triple above
# is written out rather than assumed.
#
# Read by tools/coverage-check.py and tools/trackcheck.py via TRACKS.toml.
#
# One line, the directory name under spec-data/, no leading path.

ext-identity-v3.10
